===Lizardman Canyon===
Three shamans reside in the western area of [[Lizardman Canyon]] via the [[Handholds (Lizardman Canyon)|handholds]]. These three shamans are present in a [[multi-combat area]]. Shayzien soldiers will not attack the shamans (nor will the shamans attack them), since they are busy dealing with a small group of normal [[lizardmen]]. Below are a couple ways to get there.

Players can check how many players are currently in the western area of the canyon by speaking to the wounded soldier outside the canyon, just south of the broken crossbow.

'''{{Colour|red|Warning}}:''' Be wary of more than one shaman attacking at a time as they can quickly stack up damage from their abilities and attacks, which can quickly end a trip. To avoid being attacked constantly by the nearby lizardmen and their [[lizardman brute|brute]] forms, killing the ones in the north and south-west corners is recommended.

====Xeric's talisman====
#Use [[Xeric's talisman]] to teleport to Xeric's Inferno.
#Run south through [[Lovakengj]].
#Once you've reached the south end near some [[giant bat]]s and a house with a [[water source]], head a bit west to reach some patrolling [[Kourend guard]]s.
#Go south into the [[Lizardman Canyon|canyon]] and down the handholds to the west.

====Fairy rings====
Partial completion of [[Fairytale II - Cure a Queen]] is required to use the [[fairy rings]]. A fairy ring (code {{Fairycode|DJR}}) is nearby, just south of [[Lizardman Canyon]].

===Lizardman Caves===
[[File:Lizardman Shaman location 2.png|thumb|From Xeric's Look-Out, follow the blue arrow to reach the shamans (Slayer task only).]]
Eight shamans reside inside a cave at the northern end of the [[Lizardman Settlement]] before [[Xeric's Shrine]]. This is a [[single-way combat]] area. This location requires players to be on a lizardman Slayer task. A [[dwarf multicannon]] cannot be used here.

====Xeric's talisman====
#Use [[Xeric's talisman]] to teleport to [[Mount Quidamortem|Xeric's Honour]].
#Run south-east to the [[Mountain Guide]] and travel to Shayziens' Outpost.
#Once there, head west past some [[lizardman brute]]s.
#The shamans are inside the [[Lizardman Caves]], and [[Xeric's Shrine]] is due north past the bridge.

====Fairy rings====
#Use the [[fairy ring]] code: {{Fairycode|CIR}} — requires partial completion of [[Fairytale II - Cure a Queen]].
#Run south past the farming guild.
#Run over the bridge past the Shayzien soldiers guarding the exit of the bridge.
#The shamans are inside the [[Lizardman Caves]], and [[Xeric's Shrine]] is due north past the bridge.

'''Fairy rings Lizardman Settlement - (Slayer Only Cave)'''
#Use the [[fairy ring]] code: {{Fairycode|BLS}} — requires partial completion of [[Fairytale II - Cure a Queen]].
#Run north over bridge through to Lizardman settlement.
#Run north through lizardmen brutes.
#The shamans are inside the slayer only cave with [[Captain Cleive]], there are 4 combat areas with 2 lizardman shamans each.

==Attacks==
Lizardman shamans have standard [[ranged]] and [[melee]] attacks, so one should use [[protect from missiles|Protect from Missiles]] and stand at a distance. Unlike most monsters, lizardman shamans are able to attack with melee diagonally if the player is in range.

Lizardman shamans have several special attacks that they can utilise during the fight. Excluding the spawns, these attacks do not have a cooldown so it is possible for a lizardman shaman to repeatedly use the same ability over and over again.

*A green acidic attack that will deal 25-30 damage. Wearing tiers 1-4 [[Shayzien armour]] will reduce the damage of this attack greatly; wearing a full set of [[Shayzien armour (tier 5)|tier 5 Shayzien armour]] will completely negate this damage. This attack can also inflict [[poison]] that ignores prayers starting at 10 damage.
**Players who have completed the hard [[Kourend & Kebos Diary]] can talk to [[Captain Cleive]] to be able to wear their [[Slayer helmet]] or [[Slayer helmet (i)]] instead of a [[Shayzien helm (5)]].
*A jump attack that targets a small area where the player was previously standing on. If the player is in that landing area when the shaman crashes down, they will be dealt with 20-25 [[typeless]] damage. This jump has a 3x3 AoE (2x2 in the temple, with the player's position as the north-east tile) and is not used if the jump location is obstructed.
*Lizardman shamans can summon 3 small purple [[Spawn (lizardman shaman)|spawns]] that appear next to the player (indicated by the ground shaking). After a few seconds, the spawns will explode. The damage dealt is anywhere from 5-10 depending on the player's proximity next to them; their explosion covers a 5x5 area (3x3 area in the Lizardmen Temple), or a 2 tile radius from them (1 tile in the temple).

